scenario: BT-PAIR-01
title: Bluetooth pairing and headphones
area: Bluetooth
rows: F-NET-05, F-NET-08, F-NET-26
machines: any
needs: person
prereq: A Bluetooth headset or speaker in pairing mode, within one metre.
step: Open Settings, Bluetooth and switch the adapter on.
expect: The page says the adapter is on and starts searching.
clause: F-NET-08.on
step: Choose your device in the list of found devices and press Pair.
expect: The pairing finishes (a code may be shown and must match) and the device shows as connected.
clause: F-NET-05.pair
step: Play the test tone in Settings, Sound with the Bluetooth device chosen.
expect: The tone comes out of the Bluetooth device, not the computer speakers.
clause: F-NET-26.sound
step: Walk out of range or switch the device off, then bring it back.
expect: The device reconnects on its own within a minute, or the page offers Connect.
clause: F-NET-26.reconnect
step: Press Forget on the device.
expect: It disappears from the paired list.
clause: F-NET-05.forget
